      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "25. Are the Himàlayan retreats, which are cool on ac-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "count of the spray of the waves of the Ganges, and the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "charming slabs of which are occupied by Vidyâdharas, no",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "more, that men are fond of a morsel from others (doled out)",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "with an insult ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "26. Have bulbous roots disappeared entirely from the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "valleys, or the rivulets from mountains, or have branches",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "bearing delicious fruit and yielding bark–cloth disappeared",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "from trees, that the faces of wicked men devoid of courtesy",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "are looked at in eager expectancy;—faces, the creeper-like",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "eyebrows of which are made to dance by the breeze of pride",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "at having obtained with difficulty a small sum of money ?",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "27. Arise, dear friend, let us go to the forest, where even",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "the name of big folks is not heard, whose minds mean fel-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "lows that they are, are ever distracted by inconsiderateness",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "and whose speech is marred by the effect of the disease of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "wealth—there maintain yourself now on sacred fruits and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "roots, making the earth your couch and covered with fresh",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "and plentiful barks of trees-a way of living which is",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "covetable.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "28. There are the fruits of trees obtainable at will in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "every forest without difficulty; at intervals there is the cool",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "and sweet water of sacred rivers; a bed made of the tender",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "leaves of creepers is soft to the touch; ( although these are",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "available ) mean persons do yet suffer pain at the gates of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "the rich.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "translated_stanza",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "29. Seated on a stony couch in the cavern of a mountain,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "may I, in the intervals of contemplation, recall, with an in-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "ward smile, those days which seem to be longer to one",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "experiencing the misery of (having to address) supplications",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "to the wealthy and which ( days ) appear to be shorter",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "( to one ) whose mind is tossed about by the allurement of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "sensual objects.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
